# What ships to a customer site.
#
# Git-as-deploy (ADR-001) installs the GitHub branch ARCHIVE, not the deploy.bat
# mirror -- so deploy.bat's exclusions never applied to real installs. Everything
# tracked here landed in wp-content/plugins/ on every site, and files like .md,
# .pdf and .bat are served as static assets: the internal ADRs, the provisional
# gateway contract and the local Windows path in deploy.bat were all readable at
# a public URL.
#
# export-ignore keeps these out of the archive GitHub generates, so the repo can
# keep its engineering docs while installs receive only the plugin.
#
# Never export-ignore readme.txt or the main plugin file: Plugin Update Checker
# reads both to detect and describe an update.

/docs/            export-ignore
/CLAUDE.md        export-ignore
/deploy.bat       export-ignore
/composer.json    export-ignore
/.phpcs.xml.dist  export-ignore
/.gitignore       export-ignore
/.gitattributes   export-ignore
/build-wporg.sh   export-ignore
/dist/            export-ignore
